        "title": "Synthetic Dyes: From Mauveine to the Modern Industry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The synthetic dye industry was born from a failed chemistry experiment in 1856 and within 50 years had destroyed millennia-old natural dye industries worldwide. It was also the founding event of the modern chemical industry: the same German industrial infrastructure that made synthetic dyes (BASF, Bayer, Hoechst) later produced pharmaceuticals, plastics, and — notoriously — chemical weapons."
